    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ladies and gentlemen, the truth is that the coal industry is ravaging our planet at an alarming rate. Burning coal is releasing unprecedented levels of carbon dioxide, driving climate change, and devastating ecosystems around the world. The evidence is clear: we are witnessing the irreversible consequences of coal production, from coastal erosion to wildfires, and it's not just the environment that's at stake – our health, our livelihoods, and the future of our children are all under threat.\n\nI know that many of you have written off the idea of a complete transition to clean energy, citing concerns about the impact on workers in the industry. But the truth is that this is not a zero-sum game. The coal industry's reign is coming to an end, and that presents an opportunity for us to invest in the workers who have dedicated their lives to it. We can support them through retraining programs, providing financial assistance, and creating new jobs in the clean energy sector that pay just as well, if not better. We must not let misinformation about the costs of transition hold us back from taking bold action to save our planet. We owe it to ourselves, our children, and the workers who are struggling to adapt to take control of our energy future.",
